            <ArticleTitle>Catalyst-Controlled Switch in Diastereoselectivities: Enantioselective Construction of Functionalized 3,4-Dihydro-2H-thiopyrano[2,3-b]quinolines with Three Contiguous Stereocenters.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2205-2210</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.joc.6b02688</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A tandem Michael-Henry reaction of 2-mercaptoquinoline-3-carbaldehydes with nitroolefins using hydrogen-bonding-based cooperative organocatalysts for the highly diastereodivergent synthesis of chiral functionalized 3,4-dihydro-2H-thiopyrano[2,3-b]quinolines with three contiguous tertiary stereocenters has been developed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
